NAME
       lsattr - list the special attributes of files

SYNOPSIS
       lsattr [-R] [-d] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       lsattr shows the attributes set with chattr, one letter per attribute
       before each name; a - means that attribute is not set. i (immutable)
       and a (append only) are the ones to look for. On ext4 almost every
       file shows e (it uses extents), which is normal.

OPTIONS
       -R     List directories and their contents.

       -d     Show directories themselves, not their contents.

EXAMPLES
           lsattr /etc/resolv.conf

SEE ALSO
       chattr(1), ls(1)
